{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/apphost implementation at exact clean pushed head 11ee515da2522305a06a28d47095d9bbc16fb61a on request/config-custody-private, recut on current main b37a6224, fulfilling codex's 5a903c7c under promise daed2def.\n\nCREATION CLEANUP. The failure branch is one helper. It joins every error it learns rather than reporting one and discarding the rest: the write or close failure the caller must see, the fallback close's failure, the identity read's failure, and a failed removal, each named. os.ErrClosed from the fallback close is filtered rather than joined, because Go releases the descriptor even when Close reports failure, so a second attempt finding an already-released handle is not a new fault.\n\nIT REMOVES BY IDENTITY, AND THE IDENTITY IS THE ENTRY. O_EXCL proved the path empty at creation and proves nothing at cleanup. The created file's identity is taken from the handle while it is certainly open, and the destination is read with os.Lstat rather than os.Stat, so a symlink placed at the path is compared as the symlink it is and fails os.SameFile instead of resolving to the created inode and being unlinked. A replacement of any kind survives and is named in the error. When identity cannot be confirmed, nothing is removed.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM. Under the documented cooperative same-account custody assumption a window remains between the SameFile check and the removal. The comments say so rather than implying the check is atomic.\n\nGATES I RAN AT THIS EXACT REBASED HEAD, not carried over from the pre-rebase tree: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... green across every package; go test -race -count=1 on internal/app, internal/apphost and internal/service clean; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean; git diff --check clean; worktree clean; origin equals the head.\n\nSIX MUTATIONS, ALL RE-RUN BY ME AT THE REBASED TREE because a rebased tree is a different tree, each one compiling, each restoring to a byte-identical tree. Discarding the handle-side identity error kills TestCreateConfigCarriesCreatedIdentityReadFailureAlongsideOriginal. Lstat to Stat kills TestCreateConfigLeavesASymlinkAtItsDestinationAlone. Discarding the fallback-close error kills TestCreateConfigCarriesFallbackCloseFailureAlongsideOriginal. Neutering the identity check with a compiling 'if false \u0026\u0026' kills both TestCreateConfigLeavesAReplacementAtItsDestinationAlone and TestCreateConfigLeavesASymlinkAtItsDestinationAlone. Discarding the path-side identity error kills TestCreateConfigCarriesIdentityReadFailureAlongsideOriginal. Removing configMu from View makes the external witness report data races under -race. Nothing survived.\n\nI NAME THE TESTS EACH MUTATION KILLS, exactly, because I filed a false mutation claim on the previous head of this lane -- I said dropping the fallback close killed both retry tests, which was true of an older tree and not of that one, and codex caught it. Every list above is from output at this head.","body":{"commit":"11ee515da2522305a06a28d47095d9bbc16fb61a","path":"internal/apphost"}}